{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>No man shall stand before you; the dread of you and the fear of you HaShem your Elohim will lay upon the face of all the land that you tread upon, as He spoke to you.</b> This verse has 72 letters, corresponding to the Name of 72 that goes forth; from it a known Name is derived, sought out by those who seek it, who know His great power, to bring fear upon the way. And what it says, 'as He spoke to you' — for thus the Holy One, blessed be He, promised them (Exodus 23): ״את אימתי אשלח לפניך״, and so Moses our master, peace be upon him, prayed (Exodus 15): ״תפול עליהם אימתה ופחד״ — that the attribute of judgment be drawn against the enemies for the hour and also for the future. And so is the way of the Holy One, blessed be He, with the righteous, as it is written (Psalms 91): ״כי מלאכיו יצוה לך לשמרך״, and this is the sword of the Holy One, blessed be He, which has 16 faces, that strikes the enemies; and understand this, for the sword of the Holy One, blessed be He, which has 16 faces is learned in the verse (Leviticus 26): ״והבאתי עליכם חרב״, and furthermore (Isaiah 27): ״בחרבו הקשה הגדולה והחזקה״, and likewise (Genesis 3): ״ואת להט החרב המתהפכת״, and I have already written there. And the subject of this pericah is to explain that if we keep all this commandment, which is the fulfillment of the Torah, the Holy One, blessed be He, will deliver those mighty nations into Israel's hand and they shall inherit their inheritance; therefore the pericah commands that we fear HaShem, may He be exalted — as it says (Deuteronomy 6): ״את ה' אלהיך תירא״ — and that we not fear the gentiles — as it says (Deuteronomy 7): ״לא תירא מהם״ and so on, ״לא תערוץ מפניהם״ — because fear of flesh and blood is lowliness of soul and a great deficiency in the quality of fear of HaShem, blessed be He; and one who fears and trembles before flesh and blood brings a snare and stumbling-block upon his soul and brings trouble upon himself even though it was not fitting to come upon him, whereas who is the man who fears yet sets his trust in HaShem — he escapes the trouble even though it was fitting to come upon him. And so Solomon, peace be upon him, warns man about the quality of trust (Proverbs 29): ״חרדת אדם יתן מוקש ובוטח בה' ישוגב״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Verse citation '(דברים ו')' normalized to Deuteronomy 6; '(שם ז)' to Deuteronomy 7; abbreviated forms הש\"י, ע\"ה, עכו\"ם resolved per standard conventions."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:50.112746219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}